      "writtenOn": "2020-07-13T22:01:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The lookup is roughly as follows.\n1. Check the enclosing namespace of the call site.\n2. Check the namespace of the argument types, here, \"std\" because of ostream os and \"android::hardware::keymaster\" because of AuthorizationSet set. So if you move operator \u003c\u003c to any other namespace, it can no longer be found. That is true even if you import test with \"using namespace\" or if you import AuthorizationSet into ...::test. Neither will change the lookup strategy.\n\nSo if the operator\u003c\u003c should live only here and not in autorization_set.h/cpp that you will still have to keep it in the namespace android::hardware::keymaster. You can do this by opening the sub namespace test after you defined operator\u003c\u003c.",
      "parentUuid": "5e849efc_4a50f8a8",
